{
  "note": [
    "The arena's layout (unity-game.md, The Arena): demo3d's arena-layout.json format (docs/tech-demo-3d/environment.md, Layout), copied and owned. PS.Game.Arena's ArenaLayout reads it and turns it into the one placement list that the editor's ArenaBaker builds the scene from and LevelExport rasterizes into the sim's level data, game/Content/arena.json (the bake writes it; the sim's tests check it is current).",
    "Ground (x, y) is Unity's (x, z) in metres, the arena centred on the origin; yawDeg in degrees (Unity's Euler y). size: the ground, a whole number of tileM tiles: the hero's grid, from the ground's south-west corner. Everything past a fighting ground's edge band is forest, which the level data blocks whole, so the forest bounds the arena and its groves are obstacles.",
    "seed: the scatter's seed. decorationDensity: scales edge-band and forest scatter only (spacing / sqrt(density)). edgeWidthM: the edge band's width, varied by seeded noise between the two.",
    "props: named groups of kit pieces ('pack/prefab', as in footprints.json), each with a weight; every piece must be in game/manifest.json and footprints.json. scatter: per area type (clearing, path, edge, forest), layers of {props, spacingM, scale [min, max], yawJitterDeg, chance, keepCanopyOff, dressing}. Clearing and path layers may hold only pieces that do not block.",
    "areas: {type, name?, shape, pieces?}. Shapes: center + radius (a disc), center + ring [inner, outer], from + to + width (a path), or fill (forest: everything not otherwise typed). Landmarks (at) are placed explicitly: pieces [{prop, at (from the anchor), yawDeg, scale, liftM}]; their blocking pieces block tiles. Structures are the crystal structures' sites, snapped to the hero's grid: kind courtyard (center, size [x, y], yawDeg, gaps 3 or 4 of gapM, closedSide 0 south / 1 east / 2 north / 3 west when 3), ruin-wall (from, to along a grid axis, gaps evenly spaced) or pieces (its explicit pieces only); walls come from the prop group named by walls. A ruin wall's pieces are at ground positions (it has no anchor). Anchors snap to tile centres, yaws to quarter turns, gaps to an odd number of tiles. Each set of a structure's blocking pieces that share a tile is one site, large from 6 tiles.",
    "shots: the arena stills' ground focus (at) and view width (game look's `--arena-tour`).",
    "lighting: demo3d's night (moon: elevationDeg, yawDeg, colour sRGB, intensity; trilight ambient; fog, linear in view depth from startAtFocus to endAtFocus times the camera's focus distance, or exponential with density; kitValue, RGB scales for converted kit materials by vendor name prefix; hero, the hero's light; vignette; post, the night's base post stack; flames, flickering realtime point lights on these pieces, at most maxLights, with an optional ground pool; glow, point lights baked on glowing pieces). ArenaLighting reads it; ArenaBaker places the lights and bakes the night.",
    "palettes: the zones' looks (demo3d's palettes; schedule.json's zones run neon, blossom, snow, crypt, lava), each a partial lighting object over lighting plus groundTint (linear rgb over the ground's albedo) and mist (the mist cards' colour). The runtime applies one: the moon's realtime light, ambient, fog and clear colour, vignette, the hero's light, the ground and the mist; the baked kit and its bounce keep the night's. neon, the first zone's, is the default: purple ambient and fog, magenta mist, a violet moon, a cyan hero light. Their fog is exponential, as demo3d's palettes' is in practice (its ArenaLighting resets a palette's fog mode).",
    "atmosphere: mist, low mist cards in hollows (colour sRGB, heightM, noiseScale, softM; cards {at, size [x, y], yawDeg, opacity}), merged into one mesh with Game/MistCard; runes, glowing rune circles on the ground (circles {at, radiusM, color linear, intensity}, turning turnsPerS).",
    "ground: the ground's albedo colours by type (sRGB): forest, edge, clearing and path. ArenaBaker generates the ground's albedo from them, with noise."
  ],
